.TH tkuwinico n 0.1 tkutils
.SH "tkutils::tkuwinico — build \fB.ico\fR files from Tk images"
.PP
Renders the individual icon sizes with Tk and hands the PNG payloads to \fBtclutils::tuico\fR, which assembles the container. Transparency is preserved, because the payloads are PNGs written by Tk itself.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkuwinico 0.1
.CE
.SS "The short version"
.CS
# best quality: every size rendered from the vector
tkutils::tkuwinico fromSvg logo.svg app.ico

# from a raster image (integer scaling, see the caveat below)
tkutils::tkuwinico fromPhoto $photo app.ico -sizes {32 16}

# full control: one image per size, nothing is scaled here
tkutils::tkuwinico fromPhotos [list [list 32 $big] [list 16 $small]] app.ico
.CE
.SS "Three ways to produce a size"
.PP
\fB1. From SVG — the good one.\fR Each size is rendered from the vector at its target resolution, so every step is crisp:
.CS
image create photo -file logo.svg -format {svg -scaletowidth 48}
.CE
.PP
Tk 9 has SVG built in. Under Tk 8.6 the \fBtksvg\fR package provides the same photo format; load it before calling \fBfromSvg\fR.
.PP
\fB2. From a raster image.\fR \fBfromPhoto\fR scales with Tk's \fBimage copy \-zoom/\-subsample\fR. These are integer factors sampled without interpolation, so a 256\-pixel source reduced to 16 pixels gets visibly ragged. Fine for a quick icon, not for a shipped one.
.PP
\fB3. One image per size.\fR \fBfromPhotos\fR scales nothing and simply packs what it is given — the escape hatch when you rendered the sizes elsewhere, or drew the small ones by hand.
.PP
That last point is worth taking seriously: what reads well at 256 pixels turns to mush at 16. Simplified artwork for the small steps beats any scaler.
.SS Commands
.SS "\fBfromSvg svgFile outFile ?\-sizes list?\fR"
.PP
Renders every size from the SVG and writes the \fB.ico\fR. Returns the number of bytes written. \fB\-sizes\fR defaults to \fB{256 128 64 48 32 16}\fR.
.SS "\fBfromPhoto photo outFile ?\-sizes list?\fR"
.PP
Scales one square photo image to every size. Same defaults, same return value. The source must be square.
.SS "\fBfromPhotos photos outFile\fR"
.PP
Takes a list of \fB{size photoImage}\fR pairs. Each image must already be square and match its nominal size.
.SS \fBdefaultSizes\fR
.PP
Returns the default size list, \fB{256 128 64 48 32 16}\fR.
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Sizes are sorted largest first and de\-duplicated before writing.
.IP \(bu
Images created internally are deleted again; images passed in by the caller are left alone.
.IP \(bu
Tk needs a display connection even when no window is shown. In headless builds or CI, run under \fBXvfb\fR and \fBwm withdraw .\fR.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fBerrorCode\fR is always \fB{TKUTILS TKUWINICO <REASON>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
Reason	When
\fBNOSIZES\fR	empty size list, or no images given
\fBBADSIZE\fR	size outside 1..256
\fBBADOPTION\fR	unknown option
\fBNOFILE\fR	source file not readable
\fBNOSVG\fR	SVG could not be rendered (no SVG photo format available)
\fBNOTSQUARE\fR	source image is not square
\fBSIZEMISMATCH\fR	supplied image does not match its nominal size
\fBBADENTRY\fR	entry is not a \fB{size image}\fR pair
\fBPNGFAILED\fR	Tk produced no PNG data
.TE
.PP
Container\-level problems surface with \fB{TCLUTILS TUICO ...}\fR from the underlying module.
.SS Requirements
.PP
Tcl 8.6+, Tk 8.6+, \fBtclutils::tuico\fR 0.1. For \fBfromSvg\fR: Tk 9, or Tk 8.6 with \fBtksvg\fR.
